1. Problem Statement — LeetCode 1361

You are given:

n nodes numbered from 0 to n - 1
leftChild[i] → left child of node i
rightChild[i] → right child of node i

If the value is -1, that child does not exist.

We need to determine whether all these nodes together form one valid binary tree.

For a valid binary tree:

Every node can have at most one parent
There must be exactly one root
All nodes must be connected



2. Intuition

Think about building a family tree.

Every person:

can have only one parent in this representation
there should be only one starting person → root
everyone must belong to the same family tree

So your solution checks:

Does anyone have 2 parents?
        ↓
       No

Is there exactly 1 person with no parent?
        ↓
       Yes

Starting from that person,
can I reach everyone?
        ↓
       Yes

Therefore → Valid Binary Tree



3.Logic :

I solve this problem using indegree and DFS. First, I create an indegree array to track how many parents each node has. While processing the left and right child arrays, I increment the indegree of every child.
Then I validate that no node has an indegree greater than one, because in a valid binary tree every node can have at most one parent.
Next, I find the root. The root is the only node whose indegree is zero. If I find more than one such node, it means the nodes form multiple disconnected trees, so I return false.
After finding the single root, I perform DFS starting from it and count how many nodes I can visit. If the count equals n, it means all nodes are connected and form one valid binary tree. Otherwise, some nodes are disconnected, so I return false




Code:

class Solution {
    public boolean validateBinaryTreeNodes(int n, int[] leftChild, int[] rightChild) {
        int[] indegree = new int[n];
        for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
            if(leftChild[i]!=-1){
                indegree[leftChild[i]]++;
            }
            if(rightChild[i]!=-1){
                indegree[rightChild[i]]++;
            }
        }
        int root=-1;
        for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
            if(indegree[i]==0){
                if(root!=-1){
                    return false;
                }
                root=i;
            }
            int num=indegree[i];
            if(num>1){
                return false;
            }
        }
        boolean[] visited=new boolean[n];
        int count=dfs(root,visited,leftChild,rightChild);
        return count==n;
    }
    int dfs(int root,boolean[] visited,int[] leftChild,int[] rightChild){
        if(root==-1 || visited[root]){
            return 0;
        }
        visited[root]=true;
        return 1+dfs(leftChild[root],visited,leftChild,rightChild)+dfs(rightChild[root],visited,leftChild,rightChild);
    }
}
